$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2,4-dioxo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinazoline-8-carboxylate 7 Methyl
2-amino-3-carbamoylbenzoate (3.00 g, 15.45 mmol), CDI (5.01 g, 30.90
mmol) and K2CO3 (4.48 g, 32.44 mmol) were suspended in DMF (25 mL). The
resulting suspension was heated at 90°C for 3 hours. A further equivalent
of CDI and K2CO3 were added and the mixture heated for 1 hour. The
mixture was allowed to cool to ambient temperature, diluted with water
(30 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (60 mL). The aqueous layer was
neutralized with 1.0N HCl and product precipitated out. It was collected
by filtration and washed with water. to give methyl
2,4-dioxo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinazoline-8-carboxylate (2.60 g, 76%) as a
solid. The product was carried into the next step with no further
purification. MS (ES+) = 221 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of reactant(CDI) and agent after 3 hours in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Novel Hydroxymethyl-Substituted Fused Heterocycles
