$DATUM 8-Methylquinazoline-2,4(1H,3H)-dione1,2 13 A suspension of
2-amino-3-methylbenzoic acid (5.20 g, 34.40 mmol) and urea (4.87 mL,
107.33 mmol) in NMP (50 mL) was heated to 150°C overnight. The resulting
solution was cooled to ambient temperature and poured into ice-water (50
mL) and stirred until the ice melted. The white solid was collected by
filtration, washed with water (3 x 30 mL) and dried overnight.
8-methylquinazoline-2,4(1H,3H)-dione (4.50 g, 74%) as a beige solid. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ = 2.35 (s, 3H), 7.09 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.48
(d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 10.35 (s, 1H), 11.29 (s,
1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ = 17.06, 114.49, 121.97, 124.02,
124.69, 135.89, 139.14, 150.44, 162.87. HRMS: m/z [M+H]+ calcd for
C9H9N2O2: 177.06585; found 177.06587.
