$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Symmetrical Urea
Synthesis A stainless steel autoclave (50 mL) was charged with complex 1
(0.01 mmol, 5.9 mg), amine (2 mmol), methanol (2 mmol, 81 µL), and
toluene (1.5 mL) in an argon-filled glove box. The vessel was heated to
140°C (bath temperature) under closed conditions. After 24 h, the
reaction was cooled to 0°C for 30 min. The generated H2 was carefully
released in a fumehood. n-Hexane (40 mL) was then added to the reaction
mixture. The resulting solid was collected and further washed with cold
diethyl ether to afford the corresponding product. 1,3-dibenzylurea
1,3-bis(2-ethylhexyl)urea Purification of the product was performed with
silica gel column chromatography using DCM/methanol (20:1) as an eluent.
Thick dark oil (270.1 mg, 0.951 mmol, 95%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, δ):
0.89 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 12H, 4CH3), 1.28-1.41 (m, 18H), 3.09 (d, J = 5.9 Hz,
4H, 2CH2), 4.25 (br, 2H, 2NH) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 10.92,
14.07, 23.05, 24.22, 28.94, 31.01, 39.81, 43.54, 158.44 ppm; HRMS(ESI)
calcd for C17H36N2ONa: 307.2725 Found: 307.2720 [M+Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, autoclave used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium-Catalyzed Urea Synthesis Using Methanol as the C1 Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kim, Seung Hyo; Hong, Soon Hyeok
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2016), 18(2), 212-215

